-- title:
--   Base-changed twisted Čech complex at a Hilbert-functor point
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ be a commutative ring, $n$ a natural number and $\iota_0 : Z_0 \to \mathbf{P}^n_{A_0} = \operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded ring of polynomials in $n+1$ variables over $A_0$ a closed immersion; let $K$ be a field with an $A_0$-algebra structure, $\iota_K : Z_K \to \mathbf{P}^n_K$ a closed immersion, and $e : Z_K \to Z_0$ a morphism such that the square formed by $e$, $\iota_K$ followed by the structure morphism $\pi_K$, $\iota_0$ followed by $\pi_{A_0}$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $A_0 \to K$ is cartesian, and such that $e$ followed by $\iota_0$ equals $\iota_K$ followed by `ProjSpace.map A₀ K n`. Fix $d \in \mathbb{N}$ and an $A_0$-linear map $\Theta_0$ from the degree-$d$ homogeneous forms over $A_0$ to the $0$-cochains of the presheaf `ProjSpace.twist (ι₀ ≫ ProjSpace.π A₀ n) ι₀ d` for the cover `ProjSpace.stdCoverPullback ι₀` (the preimages under $\iota_0$ of the standard charts, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}(n+1)$), assumed to be given componentwise, for homogeneous $F$ of degree $d$, each index $s$ and each $i$, by the restriction to the intersection indexed by $s$ met with the $i$-th chart of $\iota_0^\sharp$ applied to the section of $\mathcal{O}$ on $D_+(x_i)$ determined by the homogeneous localisation $F/x_i^d$. Let $h : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{N}$ and let $q$ be a point `Point K n h` of the Hilbert functor, i.e. an ideal $q.I$ of $K[x_0,\dots,x_n]$ stable under taking homogeneous components, with each module `piece q.I d` finite and projective over $K$ and of rank $h(d)$ at every prime of $K$. Assume: for every homogeneous $F$ of degree $d$ over $K$, $F \in q.I$ if and only if $\iota_K^\sharp(F/x_i^d) = 0$ for all $i$; all the quotients $\ker(d^{i+1})/\operatorname{im}(d^i)$ of the corresponding Čech complex on the $Z_K$ side are subsingletons; and every element of $\ker(d^0)$ there arises componentwise, by the same formula with $\iota_K$, from some homogeneous form $F$ of degree $d$ over $K$. Then, for the Čech complex of `ProjSpace.twist (ι₀ ≫ ProjSpace.π A₀ n) ι₀ d` on the cover `ProjSpace.stdCoverPullback ι₀` base-changed to $K$: $\ker$ of the $(i+1)$-st differential is contained in the image of the $i$-th for every $i$; $\ker$ of the $0$-th differential is contained in the image of $\Theta_0$ base-changed to $K$; and that kernel has $K$-dimension $h(d)$.
--
--   This is the fibrewise form of cohomology and flat base change for the twisting sheaf $\mathcal{O}(d)$ on a closed subscheme of projective space, phrased entirely in terms of the ordered-affine-cover Čech complex: acyclicity, generation by degree-$d$ forms and the rank $h(d)$ of the $0$-cohomology at a field-valued fibre are transported back to the base-changed complex over $A_0$. It is used in the construction of a Hilbert-functor point whose ideal is generated by prescribed forms for a flat closed immersion of finite presentation.
